<title>USA: Highlights of Senate panel's FY98 ag funds bill.</title>
<headline>Highlights of Senate panel's FY98 ag funds bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highlights of the fiscal 1998 agriculture appropriations bill approved Thursday by the U.S. Senate Appropriations Committee and sent to the floor:</p>
<p>Total for the bill was $50.5 billion, $2.6 billion less than fiscal 1997 and $1.8 billion less than requested by the White House:</p>
<p>    Program (Mln $) Approved   Requested    FY97</p>
<p>    EEP			150	   500	10</p>
<p>    GSM-102, 103	 5,700	 5,700   3,500</p>
<p>    PL-480		   889	   877     880</p>
<p>    FSIS		     591	   591     574</p>
<p>    Child Nutrition    7,769	 7,783   8,653</p>
<p>    WIC		    3,927	 4,108   3,805</p>
<p>    Food stamps	 26,051	27,551  27,618</p>
<p>    FDA-A		    949	   989     921</p>
<p>    CFTC			60	    60	55</p>
<p>    Farm Credit Admin     34	    34	37</p>
<p>A-includes $91 million in prescription drug user fees.</p>
</text>
